<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02112</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>25a518c9-d4fa-4dd6-b2e0-7ff4a7183f95</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="ec955cb5-b921-439e-9095-a01a5f6032c1" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5c4d70dc-e487-45ef-b54c-4b2011eccc9d" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="8 tickets" data-solution-options="[&quot;6 tickets&quot;, &quot;8 tickets&quot;, &quot;10 tickets&quot;, &quot;12 tickets&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The expression \(9t + 7.25\) represents the cost to purchase tickets for a concert, where \(t\) is the number of tickets. A group of friends paid $79.25 for tickets. How many tickets were bought?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="fbee7c79-87a0-445a-a892-cc8b898f7e73" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(-15t^2 + 58t + 8 = 0\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(-15t^2 + 58t + 8 = 0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-15t^2 + 58t = 8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-15t^2 + 58t = 0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(15t^2 + 58t + 8 = 0\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 2 – 4.</para>
      <blockquote>A model rocket is launched from a launchpad. The function modeling the height of the rocket, in feet, \(t\) seconds after being launched is shown.</blockquote>
      <para>\(f(t) = -15t^2 + 58t + 8\)</para>
      <para>Which equation would you solve to find the time at which the rocket hits the ground?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="af0f6d88-afdc-49c8-8cdb-39521ee2e593" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="4 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;2 seconds &quot;, &quot;3 seconds &quot;, &quot;4 seconds&quot;, &quot;5 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use a non-graphing method to find the solution to the previous equation to determine the time that has passed when the rocket hits the ground.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="77177ead-21bf-47d5-8c05-3f3b97d87f3e" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="8 feet" data-solution-options="[&quot;0 feet&quot;, &quot;2 feet&quot;, &quot;8 feet&quot;, &quot;15 feet&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>How high off the ground is the launchpad from which the rocket lifts off?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0750a278-9b95-4e76-9997-19b7297b90d3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(-3t^2 + 90t = 0\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(t(90 − 3t) = -3t^2 + 90t\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-3t^2 + 90t = 675\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-3t^2 + 90t = 0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-3t^2 + 90t = 30\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 5 – 8.</para>
      <blockquote>The expressions \(t(90 − 3t)\) and \(-3t^2 + 90t\) define the same function. The function models the number of lumens emitted by a spotlight in an art exhibit over the course of \(t\) seconds.</blockquote>
      <para>Which equation represents the time when the spotlight is not emitting any light?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.2.2 and 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e5fc91a9-34b4-455f-b981-0837a3479e43" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="0 and 30 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;0 and 30 seconds&quot;, &quot;10 and 25 seconds&quot;, &quot;Only 0 seconds&quot;, &quot;15 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>At what time(s) does the spotlight not emit any light?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3ce1ef69-1b98-4969-acd5-c48e61d1d1f3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="20 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;0 seconds&quot;, &quot;20 seconds&quot;, &quot;25 seconds&quot;, &quot;30 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The artist planned for the spotlight to emit 600 lumens at 10 seconds from the start. At what other time will the spotlight emit 600 lumens of light?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="34dd878a-a1d9-490a-bcfe-161061de6d55" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="25 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;0 seconds&quot;, &quot;10 seconds&quot;, &quot;15 seconds&quot;, &quot;25 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>At 5 seconds, the spotlight will emit 375 lumens. Find another time that the spotlight emits 375 lumens.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d1aa4d5f-093f-4b11-90d5-d40945962b23" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="$16" data-solution-options="[&quot;$8&quot;, &quot;$10&quot;, &quot;$14&quot;, &quot;$16&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> 9-10.</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para>A bowling alley models the revenue from sales in one day as a function of the cost to rent a lane per hour, \(c\). Here are two expressions defining the same revenue function.</para>
        <para>\(c(160 − 10c)\)</para>
        <para>\(160c − 10c^2\)</para>
        
      </blockquote>
      <para>According to this model, how high would the cost to rent a lane have to be for the bowling alley to make $0 in revenue?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="71966d95-aaa8-45f2-8ea8-abb97354839d" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\( c(160 − 10c) = 640\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\( c(160 − 10c) = 0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\( c(160 − 10c) = 640\\)&quot;, &quot;\\( 160c − 10c^2 + 640 = 0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\( 160c − 10c^2 = 0\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What equation can you write to determine the lane cost that would allow the bowling alley to make $640 in revenue?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.2.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
</content>
